cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this, please cite it as below."
title: "Width vs depth for fact storage in small language models (E02-E04)"
authors:
  - family-names: Killaly
    given-names: Johnathon
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnathonkillaly/width-vs-depth-facts"
abstract: >-
  Three preregistered pilots on ~21M-parameter proxy LMs (13.2M non-embedding, 40M tokens, 1,920 synthetic facts).
  At equal non-embedding parameters a wide-shallow shape stores more facts than a narrow-deep one; with an equal
  tied word table about half of the lead remains.
